  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Using a VPC (or whole new cloud) from literally any other provider than AWS would be greatly appreciated. AWS routing heavily relies on ISP networks and their interconnects resulting in highly variable quality. I live in the US east region in an area with an ISP monopoly and my connection is high in latency and packet loss to them. Non-US players will experience results even worse than mine. During off-peak hours, my connection quality to India and Australia on GCP or Azure servers is better than my connection to AWS us-west. AWS may be great for cost to compute perf, but it's a bad choice for real(ish) time applications.",
